00:59:59,930 --> 01:00:01,849
Doing everything they could
to make us join them.

1163
01:00:02,391 --> 01:00:04,185
(LOUD MUSIC PLAYING)

1164
01:00:09,523 --> 01:00:13,486
I can't find Steven.
Where are the others?

1165
01:00:14,320 --> 01:00:15,529
They're blending in.

1166
01:00:18,699 --> 01:00:20,034
Oh, crumbs.

1167
01:00:20,284 --> 01:00:23,287
It's not like the
replacements were
evil, far from it.

1168
01:00:23,370 --> 01:00:26,999
People got a lot friendlier.
That's how they do it.

1169
01:00:27,708 --> 01:00:30,461
<i>It's not an invasion,
it's a merger.</i>

1170
01:00:30,544 --> 01:00:33,506
<i>They don't want to get
rid of us, not if they
can help it.</i>

1171
01:00:33,881 --> 01:00:36,509
<i>They just want to make
us more like them.</i>

1172
01:00:36,634 --> 01:00:38,427
<i>Change the way we think.</i>

1173
01:00:38,511 --> 01:00:40,638
<i>Bring us into line
with all the others.</i>

1174
01:00:40,721 --> 01:00:42,723
<i>Become another
link in their chain.</i>

1175
01:00:43,140 --> 01:00:45,559
<i>Which is fine,
unless you say no.</i>

1176
01:00:46,727 --> 01:00:48,312
That's when you get replaced.

1177
01:00:48,395 --> 01:00:50,648
Once they get your DNA,
they've got you.

1178
01:00:50,731 --> 01:00:51,816
How do they do that?

1179
01:00:51,899 --> 01:00:53,108
BASIL: <i>Any way they like.</i>

1180
01:00:53,192 --> 01:00:59,073
<i>Blood tests, the nit nurse,
sweat, kissing, saliva on
the rim of a glass.</i>

1181
01:00:59,698 --> 01:01:02,284
Why do you think
I drink with this crazy straw?

1182
01:01:02,368 --> 01:01:03,702
Not so crazy now, is it?

1183
01:01:03,994 --> 01:01:06,956
If you're not on their side,
they'll create a version
that is.

1184
01:01:07,414 --> 01:01:11,293
<i>They can bring you back
exactly the same or even
make you young again.</i>

1185
01:01:11,752 --> 01:01:13,629
<i>It looks like you,
it even has your
memories,</i>

1186
01:01:13,712 --> 01:01:16,173
<i>but really it's just a vessel
to spread their message.</i>

1187
01:01:16,257 --> 01:01:20,511
<i>Trust, love, respect, desire.</i>

1188
01:01:20,594 --> 01:01:23,347
<i>Replaced in the name
of progress.</i>

1189
01:01:24,598 --> 01:01:27,017
So, what happens
to the people who
get replaced?

1190
01:01:27,101 --> 01:01:30,062
The empties?
Don't ask me what
happens to them.

1191
01:01:30,187 --> 01:01:31,480
Why, what happens
to the empties?

1192
01:01:31,564 --> 01:01:33,148
I told you not
to ask me that!

1193
01:01:33,232 --> 01:01:35,526
Go! Get out,
before it's too late!

1194
01:01:39,655 --> 01:01:41,657
Basil?
I said go!

1195
01:01:45,661 --> 01:01:47,121
This just can't be good.

1196
01:01:47,454 --> 01:01:50,374
Sam, who was the boy that
you liked in sixth form?
Adrian?

1197
01:01:51,166 --> 01:01:53,627
Adrian Keane. Why?

1198
01:01:54,295 --> 01:01:55,462
He's over there.

1199
01:02:04,513 --> 01:02:07,141
Hey, Sam.
How's life?

1200
01:02:11,520 --> 01:02:13,564
Sam, we have to
get out of here!
We have to get out of here!

1201
01:02:13,647 --> 01:02:15,816
Where are the others?
They're blending in.

1202
01:02:17,610 --> 01:02:19,236
Oh, fuck!

1203
01:02:21,655 --> 01:02:23,490
Gary!
No, just one
more song.

1204
01:02:23,866 --> 01:02:25,784
Gary, she's a blank!

1205
01:02:25,868 --> 01:02:27,244
Don't be so judgmental.

1206
01:02:27,328 --> 01:02:28,329
Oh, for fuck...

1207
01:02:30,664 --> 01:02:31,665
Oh, yeah.
Come on.

1208
01:02:31,874 --> 01:02:33,292
Still got it.
Enough's enough.

1209
01:02:33,542 --> 01:02:34,585
Let's go.

1210
01:02:34,668 --> 01:02:36,962
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
hold up. Hold up.
(CHUCKLES)

1211
01:02:37,296 --> 01:02:38,380
Where are you all going?

1212
01:02:38,505 --> 01:02:40,507
ALL: We're leaving.
Really? What happened?

1213
01:02:40,591 --> 01:02:42,426
Adrian Keane
was in that bar.
Prick.

1214
01:02:42,509 --> 01:02:43,969
I thought you liked
Adrian Keane.

1215
01:02:44,053 --> 01:02:45,638
Adrian Keane is dead.
Oh, God.

1216
01:02:45,721 --> 01:02:48,724
Adrian Keane died in
a motorbike accident in
Italy eight years ago.

1217
01:02:48,807 --> 01:02:50,601
Did he?
They must have
had his DNA on file.

1218
01:02:50,684 --> 01:02:52,019
That's how they were
able to replicate him.

1219
01:02:52,186 --> 01:02:54,188
They know how
to get to us, man.
They know everything.

1220
01:02:54,480 --> 01:02:56,941
They didn't know
Adrian was dead.
They knew enough to tempt us.

1221
01:02:57,024 --> 01:02:59,485
They knew these three would
fall for a bunch of girls
in school uniform.

1222
01:02:59,568 --> 01:03:02,988
Hey, who wouldn't?
Am I right?
Fuck, yeah.

1223
01:03:03,072 --> 01:03:04,114
STEVEN:
We've gotta get out of town,

1224
01:03:04,198 --> 01:03:05,616
we've gotta get beyond it
before it's too late.

1225
01:03:05,866 --> 01:03:07,576
OLIVER: Where are you
getting all this from?
STEVEN: Basil.

1226
01:03:07,660 --> 01:03:10,871
Mad Basil? He of
the Bermuda Rhombus
and the Aqua Nazis?

1227
01:03:10,955 --> 01:03:13,123
Another good name
for the band, Steve.

1228
01:03:13,207 --> 01:03:14,959
You're putting our lives
in the hands of a crazy
old man?

1229
01:03:15,042 --> 01:03:16,585
He's not crazy!
No, maybe he's not.

1230
01:03:16,752 --> 01:03:18,587
Or maybe he's a blank
trying to lure us to the
edge of town,

1231
01:03:18,671 --> 01:03:21,131
onto those dark country roads
where they can deal with us.

1232
01:03:21,215 --> 01:03:24,468
Yeah, we could end
up dead in a field.
I hate fields.

1233
01:03:24,551 --> 01:03:26,845
OLIVER:
Yes. My thoughts precisely.

1234
01:03:27,388 --> 01:03:29,306
Steven's right.
We should go.

1235
01:03:29,390 --> 01:03:30,724
No, we're going
to The Beehive.

1236
01:03:30,808 --> 01:03:32,309
Gary's plan is still
the best we have.

1237
01:03:33,185 --> 01:03:34,186
Wait a minute.

1238
01:03:36,689 --> 01:03:39,733
The 1990-model Oliver was out
of commission by this point
in the evening.

1239
01:03:41,151 --> 01:03:42,152
What are you saying?

1240
01:03:44,071 --> 01:03:46,198
I like the new you.
Huh.

1241
01:03:46,281 --> 01:03:47,282
Come on.

1242
01:03:48,784 --> 01:03:50,369
This is a mistake,
isn't it?

1243
01:03:50,452 --> 01:03:51,578
GARY: Hold up!
Just stick with me.

1244
01:03:52,413 --> 01:03:53,539
GARY: Andy, come on!

1245
01:03:55,499 --> 01:03:58,168
Here we go.
Pub number nine.
(LAUGHING)

1246
01:03:58,252 --> 01:03:59,211
Fuck yes!

1247
01:03:59,294 --> 01:04:01,755
That's the spirit, Pete!
Spirits! We should do chasers.

1248
01:04:01,880 --> 01:04:03,173
Who is this guy?

1249
01:04:03,257 --> 01:04:06,677
Come on. Andy!
It can't start without you.

1250
01:04:09,346 --> 01:04:10,347
You what?

1251
01:04:10,848 --> 01:04:12,933
We can't start without you.

1252
01:04:17,438 --> 01:04:19,857
Now then.
Whose round is it?

1253
01:04:20,107 --> 01:04:21,442
It's mine.

1254
01:04:23,068 --> 01:04:24,862
Mr. Shepherd!
Is it Mr. Shepherd?

1255
01:04:25,195 --> 01:04:29,283
Why don't you kids join me?
You look like you could
do with a drink.

1256
01:04:30,784 --> 01:04:35,789
Now, let's have a little chat
about your future, shall we,
hmm?

1257
01:04:36,040 --> 01:04:39,293
Uh, Mr. Shepherd?
Please, call me Guy.

1258
01:04:40,586 --> 01:04:41,587
All right.

1259
01:04:43,297 --> 01:04:44,298
Guy...
(BOTH SNIGGER)

1260
01:04:45,299 --> 01:04:46,675
Look at you.

1261
01:04:49,344 --> 01:04:50,429
Are you a robot?

1262
01:04:51,138 --> 01:04:53,599
Does anyone know
what robot means?

1263
01:04:53,766 --> 01:04:54,933
Yeah. I do!
Yes, Gary.

1264
01:04:55,350 --> 01:04:56,852
It means "slave."

1265
01:04:56,935 --> 01:04:58,937
Oh, very good, Gary.

1266
01:04:59,396 --> 01:05:00,856
Are you a robot, sir?

1267
01:05:00,939 --> 01:05:03,859
No, Peter, of course
I'm not a robot.

1268
01:05:03,942 --> 01:05:04,943
Sir?
Yes, Steven.

1269
01:05:05,069 --> 01:05:06,403
But you're on their
side, though?

1270
01:05:06,487 --> 01:05:09,198
This is not about
sides, Steven.

1271
01:05:09,364 --> 01:05:11,533
It's not about shirts
versus skins.

1272
01:05:11,658 --> 01:05:15,287
It's about working
together as one team.

1273
01:05:15,454 --> 01:05:18,999
I know it may seem a bit weird
and a little bit scary,

1274
01:05:19,625 --> 01:05:21,794
but please believe me,
it's quite the opposite.

1275
01:05:21,919 --> 01:05:23,462
They're here to help.

1276
01:05:23,545 --> 01:05:27,007
To straighten us out.
To prepare us
for the big league.

1277
01:05:27,341 --> 01:05:30,677
They've seen something
in us, a potential.

1278
01:05:30,803 --> 01:05:33,305
There's a vast community
of worlds up there,

1279
01:05:33,472 --> 01:05:37,726
living together, peacefully,
cooperatively.

1280
01:05:38,185 --> 01:05:41,188
And guess what?
They want us along
for the ride.

1281
01:05:43,065 --> 01:05:45,234
Pretty cool, eh, gang?
(LAUGHING)

1282
01:05:45,359 --> 01:05:47,945
So, (CLEARS THROAT)
they're not here to harm us?

1283
01:05:48,362 --> 01:05:52,449
Far from it, O-Man.
No, they're here to help.

1284
01:05:52,533 --> 01:05:55,285
I'm not saying they're
afraid to get tough.

1285
01:05:55,410 --> 01:05:58,122
I certainly had to get
tough with you in my day.

1286
01:05:58,539 --> 01:06:01,667
And what one amongst you
wouldn't thank me for it? Hmm?

1287
01:06:01,875 --> 01:06:05,170
In some respects,
they're a lot like teachers.

1288
01:06:05,254 --> 01:06:09,508
Stern, yes.
A little frightening.

1289
01:06:09,591 --> 01:06:11,135
But it's all for
our betterment.

1290
01:06:12,052 --> 01:06:18,016
So, what do you say
we all go somewhere and
talk about this properly?

1291
01:06:18,225 --> 01:06:19,351
That wasn't properly?

1292
01:06:19,434 --> 01:06:23,063
Well, I think it's pretty
clear, guys, what Mr. Shepherd
is trying to say is that...

1293
01:06:23,897 --> 01:06:25,274
(ALL GASP)

1294
01:06:25,732 --> 01:06:28,026
Andy! What the fuck?

1295
01:06:28,277 --> 01:06:30,737
Yes, Andy. What the fuck?

1296
01:06:30,946 --> 01:06:32,364
WTF?
(SCREAMS)

1297
01:06:34,283 --> 01:06:35,325
(ALARMS RINGING)

1298
01:06:35,409 --> 01:06:39,413
Humans, you leave
us no recourse.

1299
01:06:39,621 --> 01:06:42,583
If you will not
join us willingly,

1300
01:06:43,041 --> 01:06:47,004
we will be forced to use
other means of persuasion.

1301
01:06:47,087 --> 01:06:48,714
Now, please...

1302
01:06:54,553 --> 01:06:56,013
(SCREAMS)

1303
01:06:56,096 --> 01:06:57,973
I fucking hate this town!

1304
01:06:59,892 --> 01:07:01,351
(GRUNTING)

1305
01:07:13,780 --> 01:07:14,781
(SCREAMS)

1306
01:07:33,967 --> 01:07:34,968
(SCREAMING)

1307
01:07:38,597 --> 01:07:39,806
Oh, oh!

1308
01:07:47,356 --> 01:07:49,233
Oh, crumbs,
you're heavy.
Sorry.

1309
01:08:13,840 --> 01:08:15,175
Motherfucker!

1310
01:08:28,689 --> 01:08:29,690
(EXCLAIMS)

1311
01:08:34,903 --> 01:08:36,613
Andy!

1312
01:08:36,780 --> 01:08:38,156
Twist the melon, man!

1313
01:08:40,951 --> 01:08:42,369
Yeah!
(GRUNTS)

1314
01:08:44,454 --> 01:08:48,208
Sam, this is no way
for a family to behave.

1315
01:08:56,967 --> 01:08:59,386
Sam, I'm disappointed
in you.

1316
01:09:05,851 --> 01:09:07,853
O-Man!

1317
01:09:11,982 --> 01:09:13,358
(GRUNTING)

1318
01:09:22,576 --> 01:09:23,577
Okay, Andy.

1319
01:09:23,910 --> 01:09:25,245
Break it up.

1320
01:09:26,913 --> 01:09:28,540
It doesn't have
to be like this.

1321
01:09:29,750 --> 01:09:35,797
It could be so much simpler,
so completely painless.

1322
01:09:36,673 --> 01:09:38,759
If only you'd see the light.

1323
01:09:38,842 --> 01:09:40,010
OLIVER: Yes.

1324
01:09:40,093 --> 01:09:43,680
See, it's not
about conflict,

1325
01:09:45,640 --> 01:09:47,351
it's about togetherness.

1326
01:09:47,434 --> 01:09:50,562
Yes. Let's try this
again, shall we?

1327
01:09:51,146 --> 01:09:52,147
How about another round?

1328
01:09:52,731 --> 01:09:56,610
Nah, we're done here.

1329
01:09:57,402 --> 01:10:00,947
Yes, Gary, that appears
to be the case. (SNAPS)
(ALARM RINGING)

1330
01:10:01,031 --> 01:10:02,449
The Smokehouse!

1331
01:10:02,908 --> 01:10:04,159
What?
Just do it!

1332
01:10:05,118 --> 01:10:06,119
Come on!

1333
01:10:07,037 --> 01:10:08,038
This way!

1334
01:10:18,006 --> 01:10:20,842
BOTH: Humans,
this is your final warning.

1335
01:10:20,926 --> 01:10:23,220
Failure to comply
will result in your...

1336
01:10:23,303 --> 01:10:24,304
(GASPS)

1337
01:10:24,971 --> 01:10:28,433
Humans, obey now,
or face the consequences.

1338
01:10:31,812 --> 01:10:32,813
Let's go!

1339
01:10:35,148 --> 01:10:36,191
(GRUNTING)

1340
01:10:41,905 --> 01:10:43,031
Shit.

1341
01:10:43,782 --> 01:10:44,991
Oh, look, there's my car!

1342
01:10:47,828 --> 01:10:48,829
Let's climb down
the drainpipe.

1343
01:10:50,247 --> 01:10:51,790
I've got a better idea.

1344
01:10:52,833 --> 01:10:54,251
(CAR ALARM WAILING)

1345
01:10:55,293 --> 01:10:56,753
Climb down the drainpipe.

1346
01:11:00,590 --> 01:11:01,716
Okay, just go.

1347
01:11:01,800 --> 01:11:02,759
Wait. What about the others?

1348
01:11:02,843 --> 01:11:04,344
Leave 'em with me, okay?
I got this.

1349
01:11:04,386 --> 01:11:06,304
Are you sure?
Yeah, I always
land on my feet.

1350
01:11:06,847 --> 01:11:07,889
I don't know
if that's true, Gary.

1351
01:11:08,682 --> 01:11:09,683
Just go.

1352
01:11:10,225 --> 01:11:11,935
Will you find out
what happened to
my brother?

1353
01:11:12,185 --> 01:11:15,730
Yeah, of course, of course,
and I'll look after Stevie
for you, eh?

1354
01:11:16,356 --> 01:11:19,025
He's a good guy.
He's better than me.

1355
01:11:19,776 --> 01:11:23,321
Gary, you're not a bad person,
but you're not boyfriend
material.

1356
01:11:24,281 --> 01:11:26,992
The whole "free spirit quick
one in the disabled toilets"
thing

1357
01:11:27,075 --> 01:11:30,871
is kinda cool when you're 17,
but not when you're facing 40.

1358
01:11:31,872 --> 01:11:35,333
There comes a time when
you have to go forwards
and not backwards.

1359
01:11:36,376 --> 01:11:39,296
Maybe if I hadn't left you
behind that night, things
would all be different.

1360
01:11:40,213 --> 01:11:41,798
It's not all about
that night, Gary.

1361
01:11:42,757 --> 01:11:43,758
Isn't it?

1362
01:11:44,384 --> 01:11:45,677
It doesn't have to be.

1363
01:11:48,013 --> 01:11:49,723
We'll always have the
disableds, though, won't we?

1364
01:11:50,891 --> 01:11:53,435
Yeah. Yeah, we'll always
have the disableds.

1365
01:11:54,394 --> 01:11:55,645
(STARTS ENGINE)

1366
01:12:15,582 --> 01:12:16,583
Oh, no.

1367
01:12:21,546 --> 01:12:22,547
(GRUNTING)

1368
01:12:28,803 --> 01:12:30,222
STEVEN: Where's Sam?

1369
01:12:30,514 --> 01:12:31,723
I put her in her car.

1370
01:12:31,890 --> 01:12:32,933
You did what?

1371
01:12:33,058 --> 01:12:35,018
I put her in her car.
I just told her to leave.

1372
01:12:35,101 --> 01:12:37,854
You just sent away
the only one of us
sober enough to drive?

1373
01:12:37,938 --> 01:12:40,148
Yeah.
You just couldn't
stand the fact

1374
01:12:40,232 --> 01:12:41,650
that she might
prefer me to you.

1375
01:12:41,733 --> 01:12:43,401
That's not true.
It is true, Gary!

1376
01:12:43,735 --> 01:12:45,445
I was getting somewhere.
We held hands.

1377
01:12:45,695 --> 01:12:48,198
I was just trying to help!
You were trying to help
yourself, more like!

1378
01:12:48,281 --> 01:12:51,159
Jesus, I do something right
for a change and you fuckers
get on my case.

1379
01:12:51,243 --> 01:12:54,579
Wow, that's the first time
I've ever heard you admit
being wrong.

1380
01:12:54,663 --> 01:12:56,331
I said I did something right!

1381
01:12:56,414 --> 01:12:57,582
Yeah, "for a change".

1382
01:12:57,666 --> 01:12:59,793
GARY: So?
Meaning the rest of
the time you're wrong.

1383
01:12:59,876 --> 01:13:01,461
Not necessarily.

1384
01:13:01,545 --> 01:13:04,798
Look, I just thought
it was best to keep her
out of harm's way.

1385
01:13:04,881 --> 01:13:07,175
And what about us, Gary?
Aren't we in harm's way?

1386
01:13:07,259 --> 01:13:09,886
We're all right, Pete.
Come on, we're
The Five Musketeers.

1387
01:13:09,970 --> 01:13:12,055
No, we're the Four Musketeers.

1388
01:13:14,182 --> 01:13:17,644
Wait, how do we know
you put her in the car?

1389
01:13:18,395 --> 01:13:19,896
How do we know
you're you?

1390
01:13:19,980 --> 01:13:21,064
Of course I'm me!

1391
01:13:21,147 --> 01:13:24,484
Well, who the fuck
are you, Gary?
I'm Gary King.

1392
01:13:24,985 --> 01:13:27,529
There's only one Gary King.
How do I know you guys
are you?

1393
01:13:27,612 --> 01:13:28,989
We've been together
the whole time.

1394
01:13:29,239 --> 01:13:32,450
You might all not be you.
How did you know O-Man
wasn't O-Man?

1395
01:13:32,534 --> 01:13:34,452
Because his birthmark
was back.

